selector_to_html = {"a[href=\"Orifice.html#pyskyfire.ducts.orifice.Orifice.solve\"]": "<dt class=\"sig sig-object py\" id=\"pyskyfire.ducts.orifice.Orifice.solve\">\n<span class=\"sig-name descname\"><span class=\"pre\">solve</span></span><span class=\"sig-paren\">(</span><em class=\"sig-param\"><span class=\"keyword-only-separator o\"><abbr title=\"Keyword-only parameters separator (PEP 3102)\"><span class=\"pre\">*</span></abbr></span></em>, <em class=\"sig-param\"><span class=\"n\"><span class=\"pre\">inlet_state</span></span><span class=\"p\"><span class=\"pre\">:</span></span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\"><a class=\"reference internal\" href=\"../../thermo/state/FluidState.html#pyskyfire.thermo.state.FluidState\" title=\"pyskyfire.thermo.state.FluidState\"><span class=\"pre\">FluidState</span></a></span></em>, <em class=\"sig-param\"><span class=\"n\"><span class=\"pre\">mass_flow</span></span><span class=\"p\"><span class=\"pre\">:</span></span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\"><a class=\"reference external\" href=\"https://docs.python.org/3/builtins/functions.html#float\" title=\"(in Python v3.15)\"><span class=\"pre\">float</span></a></span></em>, <em class=\"sig-param\"><span class=\"n\"><span class=\"pre\">fluid</span></span></em><span class=\"sig-paren\">)</span> <span class=\"sig-return\"><span class=\"sig-return-icon\">\u2192</span> <span class=\"sig-return-typehint\"><a class=\"reference internal\" href=\"OrificeResult.html#pyskyfire.ducts.orifice.OrificeResult\" title=\"pyskyfire.ducts.orifice.OrificeResult\"><span class=\"pre\">OrificeResult</span></a></span></span></dt><dd><p>The discharge pressure that drives <code class=\"docutils literal notranslate\"><span class=\"pre\">mass_flow</span></code> through the orifice.</p></dd>", "a[href=\"OrificeCorrelationWarning.html#pyskyfire.ducts.orifice.OrificeCorrelationWarning\"]": "<dt class=\"sig sig-object py\" id=\"pyskyfire.ducts.orifice.OrificeCorrelationWarning\">\n<span class=\"property\"><span class=\"k\"><span class=\"pre\">exception</span></span><span class=\"w\"> </span></span><span class=\"sig-prename descclassname\"><span class=\"pre\">pyskyfire.ducts.orifice.</span></span><span class=\"sig-name descname\"><span class=\"pre\">OrificeCorrelationWarning</span></span></dt><dd><p>Bases: <a class=\"reference external\" href=\"https://docs.python.org/3/builtins/exceptions.html#RuntimeWarning\" title=\"(in Python v3.15)\"><code class=\"xref py py-obj docutils literal notranslate\"><span class=\"pre\">RuntimeWarning</span></code></a></p><p>A discharge-coefficient correlation is used outside its documented range.</p></dd>", "a[href=\"#module-pyskyfire.ducts.orifice\"]": "<h1 class=\"tippy-header\" style=\"margin-top: 0;\">pyskyfire.ducts.orifice<a class=\"headerlink\" href=\"#module-pyskyfire.ducts.orifice\" title=\"Link to this heading\">\u00b6</a></h1><p>Orifices: short restrictions described by a flow area and a discharge coefficient.</p><p>An <a class=\"reference internal\" href=\"Orifice.html#pyskyfire.ducts.orifice.Orifice\" title=\"pyskyfire.ducts.orifice.Orifice\"><code class=\"xref py py-class docutils literal notranslate\"><span class=\"pre\">Orifice</span></code></a> is a hole that discharges into a large volume: an injector\norifice into the chamber, a valve seat into the line behind it, a bleed into a\ncavity. Its jet\u2019s kinetic energy is not recovered, so the whole drop from the\ninlet to the discharge pressure is lost. An <a class=\"reference internal\" href=\"OrificePlate.html#pyskyfire.ducts.orifice.OrificePlate\" title=\"pyskyfire.ducts.orifice.OrificePlate\"><code class=\"xref py py-class docutils literal notranslate\"><span class=\"pre\">OrificePlate</span></code></a> is a thin\nround hole sitting in a pipe: the flow approaches it at the pipe velocity, and\npart of the drop recovers downstream as the jet re-expands to the pipe bore.\nThe plate follows ISO 5167; see its notes.</p>", "a[href=\"OrificeCapacityError.html#pyskyfire.ducts.orifice.OrificeCapacityError\"]": "<dt class=\"sig sig-object py\" id=\"pyskyfire.ducts.orifice.OrificeCapacityError\">\n<span class=\"property\"><span class=\"k\"><span class=\"pre\">exception</span></span><span class=\"w\"> </span></span><span class=\"sig-prename descclassname\"><span class=\"pre\">pyskyfire.ducts.orifice.</span></span><span class=\"sig-name descname\"><span class=\"pre\">OrificeCapacityError</span></span><span class=\"sig-paren\">(</span><em class=\"sig-param\"><span class=\"n\"><span class=\"pre\">message</span></span><span class=\"p\"><span class=\"pre\">:</span></span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\"><a class=\"reference external\" href=\"https://docs.python.org/3/builtins/stdtypes.html#str\" title=\"(in Python v3.15)\"><span class=\"pre\">str</span></a></span></em>, <em class=\"sig-param\"><span class=\"n\"><span class=\"pre\">max_mass_flow</span></span><span class=\"p\"><span class=\"pre\">:</span></span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\"><a class=\"reference external\" href=\"https://docs.python.org/3/builtins/functions.html#float\" title=\"(in Python v3.15)\"><span class=\"pre\">float</span></a></span></em><span class=\"sig-paren\">)</span></dt><dd><p>Bases: <a class=\"reference external\" href=\"https://docs.python.org/3/builtins/exceptions.html#ValueError\" title=\"(in Python v3.15)\"><code class=\"xref py py-obj docutils literal notranslate\"><span class=\"pre\">ValueError</span></code></a></p><p>The inlet state cannot drive the requested mass flow through the orifice.</p><p>Either the flow chokes below the requested mass flow, or passing it would\nneed a discharge pressure below the searched floor. <code class=\"docutils literal notranslate\"><span class=\"pre\">max_mass_flow</span></code> is\nthe largest flow found [kg/s].</p></dd>", "a[href=\"#pyskyfire.ducts.orifice.required_area\"]": "<dt class=\"sig sig-object py\" id=\"pyskyfire.ducts.orifice.required_area\">\n<span class=\"sig-prename descclassname\"><span class=\"pre\">pyskyfire.ducts.orifice.</span></span><span class=\"sig-name descname\"><span class=\"pre\">required_area</span></span><span class=\"sig-paren\">(</span><em class=\"sig-param\"><span class=\"keyword-only-separator o\"><abbr title=\"Keyword-only parameters separator (PEP 3102)\"><span class=\"pre\">*</span></abbr></span></em>, <em class=\"sig-param\"><span class=\"n\"><span class=\"pre\">mass_flow</span></span></em>, <em class=\"sig-param\"><span class=\"n\"><span class=\"pre\">inlet_state</span></span></em>, <em class=\"sig-param\"><span class=\"n\"><span class=\"pre\">dp</span></span></em>, <em class=\"sig-param\"><span class=\"n\"><span class=\"pre\">fluid</span></span></em>, <em class=\"sig-param\"><span class=\"n\"><span class=\"pre\">cd</span></span></em><span class=\"sig-paren\">)</span> <span class=\"sig-return\"><span class=\"sig-return-icon\">\u2192</span> <span class=\"sig-return-typehint\"><a class=\"reference external\" href=\"https://docs.python.org/3/builtins/functions.html#float\" title=\"(in Python v3.15)\"><span class=\"pre\">float</span></a></span></span></dt><dd><p>Geometric area that passes <code class=\"docutils literal notranslate\"><span class=\"pre\">mass_flow</span></code> with a pressure drop <code class=\"docutils literal notranslate\"><span class=\"pre\">dp</span></code> [m\u00b2].</p><p>The inverse of <a class=\"reference internal\" href=\"Orifice.html#pyskyfire.ducts.orifice.Orifice.solve\" title=\"pyskyfire.ducts.orifice.Orifice.solve\"><code class=\"xref py py-meth docutils literal notranslate\"><span class=\"pre\">Orifice.solve()</span></code></a>, for any hole shape: the orifice\ndischarges at <code class=\"docutils literal notranslate\"><span class=\"pre\">inlet_state.p</span> <span class=\"pre\">-</span> <span class=\"pre\">dp</span></code>, with discharge coefficient <code class=\"docutils literal notranslate\"><span class=\"pre\">cd</span></code>.</p></dd>", "a[href=\"#module-contents\"]": "<h2 class=\"tippy-header\" style=\"margin-top: 0;\">Module Contents<a class=\"headerlink\" href=\"#module-contents\" title=\"Link to this heading\">\u00b6</a></h2>", "a[href=\"#exceptions\"]": "<h2 class=\"tippy-header\" style=\"margin-top: 0;\">Exceptions<a class=\"headerlink\" href=\"#exceptions\" title=\"Link to this heading\">\u00b6</a></h2>", "a[href=\"OrificeResult.html#pyskyfire.ducts.orifice.OrificeResult\"]": "<dt class=\"sig sig-object py\" id=\"pyskyfire.ducts.orifice.OrificeResult\">\n<span class=\"property\"><span class=\"k\"><span class=\"pre\">class</span></span><span class=\"w\"> </span></span><span class=\"sig-prename descclassname\"><span class=\"pre\">pyskyfire.ducts.orifice.</span></span><span class=\"sig-name descname\"><span class=\"pre\">OrificeResult</span></span></dt><dd><p>States and diagnostics of the flow through an orifice.</p><p><code class=\"docutils literal notranslate\"><span class=\"pre\">throat_state</span></code> is the ideal isentropic state at the vena contracta and\n<code class=\"docutils literal notranslate\"><span class=\"pre\">velocity</span></code> the ideal jet velocity there [m/s]. The real jet is slower by\nthe velocity coefficient, which the discharge coefficient includes but\ndoes not separate out. <code class=\"docutils literal notranslate\"><span class=\"pre\">outlet_state</span></code> is at the discharge pressure with\nthe inlet enthalpy: the jet\u2019s kinetic energy has been dissipated.\n<code class=\"docutils literal notranslate\"><span class=\"pre\">choked</span></code> is True when the discharge pressure lies below the pressure at\nwhich the ideal mass flux peaks, so lowering it further adds no flow.</p></dd>", "a[href=\"Orifice.html#pyskyfire.ducts.orifice.Orifice\"]": "<dt class=\"sig sig-object py\" id=\"pyskyfire.ducts.orifice.Orifice\">\n<span class=\"property\"><span class=\"k\"><span class=\"pre\">class</span></span><span class=\"w\"> </span></span><span class=\"sig-prename descclassname\"><span class=\"pre\">pyskyfire.ducts.orifice.</span></span><span class=\"sig-name descname\"><span class=\"pre\">Orifice</span></span><span class=\"sig-paren\">(</span><em class=\"sig-param\"><span class=\"n\"><span class=\"pre\">area</span></span></em>, <em class=\"sig-param\"><span class=\"keyword-only-separator o\"><abbr title=\"Keyword-only parameters separator (PEP 3102)\"><span class=\"pre\">*</span></abbr></span></em>, <em class=\"sig-param\"><span class=\"n\"><span class=\"pre\">cd</span></span></em>, <em class=\"sig-param\"><span class=\"n\"><span class=\"pre\">hydraulic_diameter</span></span><span class=\"o\"><span class=\"pre\">=</span></span><span class=\"default_value\"><span class=\"pre\">None</span></span></em>, <em class=\"sig-param\"><span class=\"n\"><span class=\"pre\">length</span></span><span class=\"o\"><span class=\"pre\">=</span></span><span class=\"default_value\"><span class=\"pre\">0.0</span></span></em><span class=\"sig-paren\">)</span></dt><dd><p>A short restriction discharging into a large volume.</p><p class=\"rubric\">Notes</p><p>Use <a class=\"reference internal\" href=\"#pyskyfire.ducts.orifice.Orifice.circular\" title=\"pyskyfire.ducts.orifice.Orifice.circular\"><code class=\"xref py py-meth docutils literal notranslate\"><span class=\"pre\">circular()</span></code></a>, <a class=\"reference internal\" href=\"#pyskyfire.ducts.orifice.Orifice.annular\" title=\"pyskyfire.ducts.orifice.Orifice.annular\"><code class=\"xref py py-meth docutils literal notranslate\"><span class=\"pre\">annular()</span></code></a> or <a class=\"reference internal\" href=\"#pyskyfire.ducts.orifice.Orifice.slot\" title=\"pyskyfire.ducts.orifice.Orifice.slot\"><code class=\"xref py py-meth docutils literal notranslate\"><span class=\"pre\">slot()</span></code></a> for those shapes.\nThe generic constructor takes any area, so an effective area quoted as\n<code class=\"docutils literal notranslate\"><span class=\"pre\">Cd\u00b7A</span></code> can be given as <code class=\"docutils literal notranslate\"><span class=\"pre\">Orifice(area=CdA,</span> <span class=\"pre\">cd=1.0)</span></code>.</p></dd>", "a[href=\"../../thermo/eos/EquationOfState.html#pyskyfire.thermo.eos.EquationOfState\"]": "<dt class=\"sig sig-object py\" id=\"pyskyfire.thermo.eos.EquationOfState\">\n<span class=\"property\"><span class=\"k\"><span class=\"pre\">class</span></span><span class=\"w\"> </span></span><span class=\"sig-prename descclassname\"><span class=\"pre\">pyskyfire.thermo.eos.</span></span><span class=\"sig-name descname\"><span class=\"pre\">EquationOfState</span></span></dt><dd><p>Bases: <a class=\"reference external\" href=\"https://docs.python.org/3/library/abc.html#abc.ABC\" title=\"(in Python v3.15)\"><code class=\"xref py py-obj docutils literal notranslate\"><span class=\"pre\">abc.ABC</span></code></a></p><p>The state lookups a machine design asks of a fluid.</p><p>Every pressure is in Pa, temperature in K and specific enthalpy in\nJ kg\u207b\u00b9. Enthalpy is only ever compared with enthalpy from the same\nequation of state, so its datum does not matter.</p></dd>", "a[href=\"OrificePlateResult.html#pyskyfire.ducts.orifice.OrificePlateResult\"]": "<dt class=\"sig sig-object py\" id=\"pyskyfire.ducts.orifice.OrificePlateResult\">\n<span class=\"property\"><span class=\"k\"><span class=\"pre\">class</span></span><span class=\"w\"> </span></span><span class=\"sig-prename descclassname\"><span class=\"pre\">pyskyfire.ducts.orifice.</span></span><span class=\"sig-name descname\"><span class=\"pre\">OrificePlateResult</span></span></dt><dd><p>Bases: <code class=\"xref py py-obj docutils literal notranslate\"><span class=\"pre\">OrificeResult</span></code></p><p>An <code class=\"xref py py-class docutils literal notranslate\"><span class=\"pre\">OrificeResult</span></code> with the plate\u2019s metering quantities.</p><p><code class=\"docutils literal notranslate\"><span class=\"pre\">throat_state</span></code> is at the downstream tap, and\n<a class=\"reference internal\" href=\"#pyskyfire.ducts.orifice.OrificePlateResult.differential_pressure\" title=\"pyskyfire.ducts.orifice.OrificePlateResult.differential_pressure\"><code class=\"xref py py-attr docutils literal notranslate\"><span class=\"pre\">differential_pressure</span></code></a> is the tap-to-tap drop a flow meter reads.\n<code class=\"docutils literal notranslate\"><span class=\"pre\">outlet_state</span></code> is where the flow has recovered to the pipe bore, so\n<code class=\"xref py py-attr docutils literal notranslate\"><span class=\"pre\">pressure_loss</span></code> is the permanent loss, which is smaller.</p></dd>", "a[href=\"#functions\"]": "<h2 class=\"tippy-header\" style=\"margin-top: 0;\">Functions<a class=\"headerlink\" href=\"#functions\" title=\"Link to this heading\">\u00b6</a></h2>", "a[href=\"#classes\"]": "<h2 class=\"tippy-header\" style=\"margin-top: 0;\">Classes<a class=\"headerlink\" href=\"#classes\" title=\"Link to this heading\">\u00b6</a></h2>", "a[href=\"OrificePlate.html#pyskyfire.ducts.orifice.OrificePlate\"]": "<dt class=\"sig sig-object py\" id=\"pyskyfire.ducts.orifice.OrificePlate\">\n<span class=\"property\"><span class=\"k\"><span class=\"pre\">class</span></span><span class=\"w\"> </span></span><span class=\"sig-prename descclassname\"><span class=\"pre\">pyskyfire.ducts.orifice.</span></span><span class=\"sig-name descname\"><span class=\"pre\">OrificePlate</span></span><span class=\"sig-paren\">(</span><em class=\"sig-param\"><span class=\"n\"><span class=\"pre\">pipe_diameter</span></span></em>, <em class=\"sig-param\"><span class=\"n\"><span class=\"pre\">orifice_diameter</span></span></em>, <em class=\"sig-param\"><span class=\"keyword-only-separator o\"><abbr title=\"Keyword-only parameters separator (PEP 3102)\"><span class=\"pre\">*</span></abbr></span></em>, <em class=\"sig-param\"><span class=\"n\"><span class=\"pre\">cd</span></span><span class=\"o\"><span class=\"pre\">=</span></span><span class=\"default_value\"><span class=\"pre\">None</span></span></em>, <em class=\"sig-param\"><span class=\"n\"><span class=\"pre\">taps</span></span><span class=\"o\"><span class=\"pre\">=</span></span><span class=\"default_value\"><span class=\"pre\">'flange'</span></span></em>, <em class=\"sig-param\"><span class=\"n\"><span class=\"pre\">thickness</span></span><span class=\"o\"><span class=\"pre\">=</span></span><span class=\"default_value\"><span class=\"pre\">0.0</span></span></em><span class=\"sig-paren\">)</span></dt><dd><p>A thin round orifice plate in a straight pipe.</p><p class=\"rubric\">Notes</p><p>The flow follows ISO 5167,\n<span class=\"math notranslate nohighlight\">\\(\\dot m = C \\varepsilon A \\sqrt{2 \\rho_1 \\Delta p / (1 - \\beta^4)}\\)</span>,\nwith <a class=\"reference internal\" href=\"#pyskyfire.ducts.orifice.OrificePlate.expansibility\" title=\"pyskyfire.ducts.orifice.OrificePlate.expansibility\"><code class=\"xref py py-meth docutils literal notranslate\"><span class=\"pre\">expansibility()</span></code></a> for \u03b5. That \u03b5 is fitted to thin plates, whose\njet keeps contracting past the bore, and it is not the isentropic nozzle\nexpansion <code class=\"xref py py-class docutils literal notranslate\"><span class=\"pre\">Orifice</span></code> uses: for a gas at a 2.5 % tap drop the\nnozzle expansion would overstate the drop by about 1.6 %.</p><p>The permanent loss is ISO 5167-1\u2019s recovery relation,</p></dd>"}
skip_classes = ["headerlink", "sd-stretched-link"]

window.onload = function () {
    for (const [select, tip_html] of Object.entries(selector_to_html)) {
        const links = document.querySelectorAll(` ${select}`);
        for (const link of links) {
            if (skip_classes.some(c => link.classList.contains(c))) {
                continue;
            }

            tippy(link, {
                content: tip_html,
                allowHTML: true,
                arrow: true,
                placement: 'auto-start', maxWidth: 600, interactive: false,
                onShow(instance) {MathJax.typesetPromise([instance.popper]).then(() => {});},
            });
        };
    };
    console.log("tippy tips loaded!");
};
